The xboxrecomp toolkit
----------------------

The build compiles in the xboxrecomp toolkit (https://github.com/apexJCL/xboxrecomp,
a fork of https://github.com/sp00nznet/xboxrecomp). The toolkit is not part of
this repository. It is MIT licensed, except for the files listed in its own
NOTICE.

Those exceptions include LGPL-2.1-or-later code extracted from xemu
(https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu): the MCPX APU sources under src/apu/
(apu_core.c, apu_dsp.c, apu_vp.c and their headers) and the NV2A files
src/nv2a/nv2a_regs.h, src/nv2a/nv2a_core.c and src/nv2a/nv2a_state.h,
copyright espes, Jannik Vogel and Matt Borgerson. The toolkit's
LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt has the full licence text.

The toolkit's libraries are linked statically into blinx1_recomp. This matters
if you distribute a built binary. The LGPL then requires you to do the
following:

  - keep the copyright notices and the LGPL text with the binary;
  - make the source of the LGPL parts available, including your changes to them;
  - let recipients relink the program against a modified version of those parts,
    for example by providing the object files of the rest of the program, or all
    of its source.

Distributing this repository and the toolkit as source meets these terms. A
binary distribution must meet them separately.

This game builds with -DXBOXRECOMP_ENHANCE=ON, so the binary also contains
the toolkit's vendored enhancements overlay: microui (MIT), stb_truetype
(MIT) and the Atkinson Hyperlegible font (SIL Open Font License 1.1),
embedded as it is. Their texts are in the toolkit's LICENSES/
(MIT-microui.txt, MIT-stb.txt, OFL-1.1-atkinson-hyperlegible.txt).


dsp56300
--------

This game builds the toolkit with -DXBOXRECOMP_APU_DSP=ON (game.toml,
[build] stock_cmake), so every build links the prebuilt dsp56300 library
(https://github.com/xemu-project/dsp56300, v1.0.0, MIT, copyright 2026 Matt
Borgerson) and the Rust standard library and crates it bundles (Apache-2.0
with the LLVM exception, MIT, Unicode-3.0, Zlib; none GPL or LGPL). The
toolkit's NOTICE lists every crate, and its LICENSES/ has the texts:
LICENSES/MIT-dsp56300.txt for dsp56300 itself and
LICENSES/THIRDPARTY-dsp56300-emu.txt for the bundled crates. A binary
distribution must carry both.

Configure downloads the library, pinned by sha256 in the toolkit's
cmake/dsp56300.cmake. An offline build points XBOXRECOMP_DSP56300_ARCHIVE
at a local copy of that archive; a failed download stops the configure step.
The device runs by default; RECOMP_APU_DSP=0 goes back to the stub.


Game data
---------

BLiNX: the time sweeper is not part of this repository. No game files, assets,
saves or recompiled game code are included. You need your own copy of the game
to build and run it.
